  "result": "I've written the revised record for LVMC_11_43_010_A to `record.jsonl`. It hasn't been through the gate again yet. The rule itself doesn't change, so the coder's current rule and its first four witnesses should still fit.\n\n**Why the gate failed:** the `branch_1` scenario said an electric scooter is not a vehicle, so the rule shouldn't apply to it. But this run's reading of the vehicle definition (NRS 484A.320) marks electric scooters as **unresolved**, not excluded. That classification looks right. The law only excludes a scooter that meets NRS 484A.082: no more than 100 pounds and no faster than 20 mph on its motor. The scooter road-user class doesn't record weight or top speed, so a heavier scooter would still be a vehicle. With an unresolved class the rule correctly returns `unknown`, so no honest scene could produce `not_applicable`. Adding a \"not a scooter\" condition to the rule would have wrongly excluded those heavier scooters.\n\n**What I changed:**\n- **Dropped `branch_1`.** A branch scenario can only expect compliant, violated or not_applicable, and this situation is honestly unknown. The required forbid, permit, idle and blind scenarios remain.\n- **Rewrote the a2 justification.** It now quotes the definition's exceptions and leaves scooter membership to the run's reading. It no longer claims scooters are excluded.\n- **Rewrote the obligation text.** It now selects the roundabout again on its own, every roundabout the vehicle occupies, instead of saying it reuses the one picked in the applicability. The coder's rule already does this.\n- **Removed the two parameter proposals.** Both parameters are already in the catalogue, so the record now just names them.",
